      "title": "DCT2000: convert the file character count to a record byte count.",
      "message": "DCT2000: convert the file character count to a record byte count.\n\nFor comments, the number of characters in the comment is the number of\nbytes in the corresponding record.\n\nFor non-comments, the number of characters in the comment is *twice* the\nnumber of bytes in the corresponding record, as the characters are hex\ndigits, and there are two hex digits per byte.\n\nUse *that*, rather than the character count, in subsequent code, to make\nit a bit clearer what we're doing.\n",
